Z||000010||Screwie||12-24-2001||06:19 AM||||The "Chicago edition" of Midtown Madness, is Midtown Madness 1, so I could export it for that one as well. I don't know if there's a poly limit there, but when I've finished it for MM2, I might make a version for MM1 as well. But like I said, that depends a bit on the compatibility.<P>I can export it to a lot of game formats, and also 3dmax. I'm making this one in a program called Zmodeler (yup it's spelled wrong, but that's what it's called, a Russian guy made it  <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/biggrin.gif">)<P>I'm trying to make this one as real as possible, with a lot of detail. I hate it as well when you see a 3d model, which is supposed to be a certain car, but doesn't even look like it. I still have to make the exhaust and other stuff. Then I have to see if I can make the "Pontiac" part light up in the dark. Anyways, it'll take me a while, but I want to do it right  <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/biggrin.gif"><BR>||||reg||1
Z||000011||Screwie||12-26-2001||11:05 AM||||Well, here's the first ingame shot of the Fiero!(in Midtown Madness 2) No textures or anything yet, haven't really tweaked anything, just to see if it works ingame already. And it does  <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/biggrin.gif"><P> <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/uploads/fieroingame.jpg"> ||||reg||1
Z||000012||MinnGreenGT||12-26-2001||11:14 AM||||Cool... I can't wait to see your finished model!  <P>I started making a pickup truck for 3DMax a little more than a year ago for a school project. I ended up with an A on the project (compared to a few other projects, it was better <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/smile.gif">) But I know a ton of time & effort goes into a model.  Especially a good one.  Keep up the good work!<P>------------------<BR>              <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/uploads/GreenGT6.gif"> ||||reg||1
Z||000013||Tigger||12-26-2001||12:14 PM||||For the texturing, some might call it cheating, take several pictures of a fastback, side, front, rear, and then overlay them over the model.  Tweak whatever you need.  It will make it look real!<P>Looks Great!||||reg||14
Z||000014||Screwie||12-26-2001||02:51 PM||||For the texturing on the Corvette I made, I used photos as well. I don't think it's cheating, makes it look so much more realistic, especially when the 3d mesh isn't very detailed. But it's hard to choose what I'm going to do with this Fiero. Color, rims, scoops etc.<P>I'm thinking about these rims, haven't chosen yet:<BR> <IMG SRC="http://www.transwheel.com/limages/GW35.jpg"> <P>or<P> <IMG SRC="http://www.transwheel.com/limages/GW21.jpg"> <P>I'll leave it as stock as possible I think  <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/biggrin.gif">||||reg||1
